<article class="env-lemma" id="04Y9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04Y9">Lemma <span data-tag="04Y9">100.4.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. Every point of $|\mathcal{X}|$ has a fundamental system of quasi-compact open neighbourhoods. In particular $|\mathcal{X}|$ is locally quasi-compact in the sense of Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0068" data-tag="0068">5.13.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from the fact that there exists a scheme $U$ and a surjective, open, continuous map $U \to |\mathcal{X}|$ of topological spaces. Namely, if $U \to \mathcal{X}$ is surjective and smooth, then Lemma <a href="/tag/04XL" data-tag="04XL">100.4.7</a> guarantees that $|U| \to |\mathcal{X}|$ is continuous, surjective, and open. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>